<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Koch Hajo</h1><p class="st-meta">1581 CE – 1616 CE (approx.) · capital Hajo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The eastern half of the divided Koch kingdom, ruled from Hajo in western Assam until it fell to the Mughals.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Koch kingdom reached its height under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nara-narayan">Nara Narayan</a> and his brother and general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chilarai">Chilarai</a> in the mid 16th century. In 1581 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nara">Nara</a> Narayan divided the realm, giving the lands east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sankosh-river">Sankosh</a> river to Chilarai's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raghudev-narayan">Raghudev</a>, who ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hajo">Hajo</a> on the north bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmaputra">Brahmaputra</a>. The western half became <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cooch-behar-state">Koch Bihar</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Koch <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hajo">Hajo</a> was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> kingdom whose rulers patronised the Hayagriva Madhava temple at Hajo and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamakhya-temple">Kamakhya</a> temple near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guwahati">Guwahati</a>, which the Koch had rebuilt. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raghudev-narayan">Raghudev</a> and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parikshit-narayan">Parikshit Narayan</a> were rivals of their <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cooch-behar-state">Koch Bihar</a> cousins, who allied with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>, while Koch Hajo looked to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ahom-kingdom">Ahom kingdom</a> for support.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Mughal armies, aided by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cooch-behar-state">Koch Bihar</a>, defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parikshit-narayan">Parikshit Narayan</a> in 1613, and by 1616 Koch <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hajo">Hajo</a> was annexed. The territory became a battleground between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahom-people">Ahoms</a> until the Ahoms secured it after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-itakhuli">Battle of Itakhuli</a> in 1682.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1581 CE – 1616 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:91.16%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1581 CE – 1616 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Hajo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Raghudev, Parikshit Narayan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Assamese, Kamtapuri</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Koch Hajo, Eastern Koch kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1598&amp;focus=koch-hajo" aria-label="Koch Hajo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7096 1214 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Koch Hajo lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7416 1470L7360 1467M7416 1470L7018 1385"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7360 1467h0M7018 1385h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7416 1470h0